Here's a detailed explanation of the code along with its output:

The `nextDayStockPrice` method calculates the price of the stock on the next day based on the given prices for the previous 8 days.

```java
public int nextDayStockPrice(int[] prices, int daysToGetTomorrow) {
    if (daysToGetTomorrow > 0) {
        // Calculate the future prices by multiplying the last two elements and dividing by 100
        return prices[prices.length - 1] + ((prices[prices.length - 2] * (double) prices[prices.length - 3]) / (100.0 * (double) prices[prices.length - 4]));
    } else {
        int[] futurePrices = new int[prices.length];
        // Calculate the future prices using dynamic programming
        for (int i = 0; i < prices.length; i++) {
            if (i == 0)
                futurePrices[i] = prices[i + 1];  // Base case: no previous days to consider
            else
                futurePrices[i] = futurePrices[i - 1] + ((futurePrices[i - 2] * (double) futurePrices[i - 3]) / (100.0 * (double) futurePrices[i - 4]));
        }
        // Find the maximum price among all days in the future prices
        return findMax(futurePrices);
    }
}
